menu "BioMess firmware"

config BIOMESS_SERIAL_NUMBER
	string "BioMess serial number"
	default "BM-NRF5340-00"
	help
	  Human-readable device serial exposed over the BioMess BLE serial
	  characteristic. Set this per board together with CONFIG_BT_DEVICE_NAME,
	  for example Messi-02.

config MYOHM_EXCITATION_MVPP
	int "AD5941 excitation DAC amplitude (mV peak-to-peak)"
	range 50 800
	default 800
	help
	  Default sweep amplitude written to AppBIACfg.DacVoltPP, in mV
	  peak-to-peak at the HSDAC, before the x2 excitation buffer gain
	  (EXCITBUFGAIN_2). The voltage at CE0 is twice this value and the
	  current into I+ is limited by the 1 kohm series resistor RL1.

	  800 keeps the setting used for all published Myohm data: 1.6 V pp at
	  CE0 (0.57 mA rms into a short), outside the +/-607 mV range over
	  which the AD5941 output is specified. 500 is the recommended value
	  for measurements on people: 1.0 V pp at CE0, 0.35 mA rms into a
	  short. BLE clients can override the value through characteristic
	  0xC018; the override is kept in RAM and returns to this default
	  after a reset.

config MYOHM_CONTACT_HIGH_OHMS
	int "Contact check threshold for a high two-wire impedance (ohms)"
	range 100 1000000
	default 3000
	help
	  BLE command 0x0B measures the two-wire impedance between electrode
	  pairs at 10 kHz and 100 kHz. An entry whose magnitude, after
	  subtracting the board series elements (RL1 and the 4.7 uF coupling
	  capacitors), exceeds this threshold is flagged as high contact.
	  Each pair includes two contacts plus the tissue between them. The
	  default sits between a pair of 1 kohm contacts (about 2 kohm) and a
	  single 4.99 kohm contact (above 5 kohm) on the AD5940 Z test board.

endmenu

source "Kconfig.zephyr"
